# Copy to .env before `make run`. The builder and worker read it as their
# environment, and docker compose reads VIRTUAL_HOST and LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL to
# wire up the proxy — so the file has to exist even if everything in it is
# left at its default.
#
# Nothing here is needed to run locally: docker-compose.dev.yml is nginx over
# the working tree, and the builder and worker run on the host from npm.

# The hostname nginx-proxy answers on, and the certificate it requests.
VIRTUAL_HOST=transit.example.org
LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=you@example.org

# Image tag to run. `make` derives this from the commit and passes it in;
# set it here only to pin a deploy to something other than HEAD.
#IMG_TAG=sha-abc1234

# How often the builder looks for a new feed. Six fields — this is `cron`'s
# second-resolution form, not crontab's five.
#BUILD_SCHEDULE=0 */10 * * * *

# Heartbeats, if you run a monitor. All five are optional and a missed ping
# never fails the work that was being reported on.
#
# The builder appends `/start` before a run, nothing on success, and `/fail`
# when a build throws — healthchecks.io's convention. Give a service that does
# not route those suffixes a plain base URL: a failed build then reaches you by
# missing its success ping rather than by reporting one.
#
# The build beat fires every BUILD_SCHEDULE — every ten minutes by default —
# including on the cycles that publish nothing because the feed and the version
# are both unchanged. That is what makes it safe to put on a periodic monitor.
#HEARTBEAT_BUILD=https://uptime.example.org/ping/build
#
# Tiles are the exception: the pipeline is skipped whenever a release can reuse
# the previous one's map, so this beat can go weeks between pings and will make
# a periodic monitor cry wolf. Leaving it unset costs nothing — a tile failure
# throws, and the build's `/fail` reports it.
#HEARTBEAT_TILES=https://uptime.example.org/ping/tiles

# The worker's three, one per realtime feed. Each fires after its data is
# stored, so a monitor that is down cannot cost a tick.
#
# Mind the cadences: the site is only live because these run, but the first two
# run every second — roughly 86,400 pings a day each — which is more than some
# hosted monitors expect to receive.
#
# Every second:
#VEHICLE_POSITIONS_HEARTBEAT_URL=https://uptime.example.org/ping/vehicles
#TRIP_UPDATES_HEARTBEAT_URL=https://uptime.example.org/ping/trips
# Hourly:
#SERVICE_ALERTS_HEARTBEAT_URL=https://uptime.example.org/ping/alerts

# Use a map bundle someone else built instead of running the tile pipeline.
# A production host should not need this; it is how a machine without Python,
# a JRE and loom still assembles a release.
#TILES_FROM=tiles/out/web

# Overrides the commit as the release's version. CI builds from a checkout
# with no git history, which is what this is for.
#APP_VERSION=
